# TECH STACK & ARCHITECTURE
- Stack: React 19 (SPA), Vite, Tailwind CSS v4, Lucide React, Supabase JS SDK (@supabase/supabase-js).
- Styling: Use '@tailwindcss/vite' plugin in vite.config.js. Main CSS entry (src/index.css) must contain only '@import "tailwindcss";'[cite: 1]. Do not create tailwind.config.js or postcss.config.js[cite: 1].
- Client Isolation: Initialize and export Supabase client strictly from 'src/lib/supabase.js' using 'import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_URL' and 'import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY'[cite: 1].

# LOCALIZATION & ENCODING (fr-CA)
- Codebase Language: Code, variables, database entities, file names, and internal comments must be in English[cite: 1].
- UI Language: 100% of user-facing UI text, button labels, table headers, form placeholders, toasts, modal dialogs, and error messages MUST be in natural Quebec French (fr-CA).
- Centralized Dictionary: Keep all UI strings and translations centralized in 'src/locales/fr.json'[cite: 6]. Components must pull labels from this dictionary rather than hardcoding raw strings.
- Enums & Formats: Never render raw DB enums (e.g., map PAID -> "Payé", UNPAID -> "En attente de paiement", DRAFT -> "Brouillon", ACTIVE -> "En cours")[cite: 1, 3]. Currency: "0,00 $ CAD"[cite: 1, 3]. Dates: French Canadian standard (YYYY-MM-DD or 'D MMMM YYYY')[cite: 3].
- File Encoding: All source files, JSX components, and JSON dictionaries MUST strictly be authored and saved in UTF-8 (without BOM). Never allow terminal tools to re-encode accented French characters into Windows-1252/ANSI.

# DATABASE DESIGN & SECURITY
- Target Output: All schema updates, triggers, and RLS policies must be appended to 'supabase/schema.sql'[cite: 1].
- Auth Architecture: Sync 'auth.users' to 'public.profiles' via an automated trigger on insert[cite: 1]. Root Admin is hardcoded to 'yulmixalabedaine@gmail.com'[cite: 1].
- Row Level Security: Enable RLS on every table[cite: 1]. Provide explicit SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE policies for authenticated users and admins[cite: 1]. Prevent self-privilege escalation on 'is_admin'[cite: 4].

# SYSTEM OS (WINDOWS POWERSHELL 5.1 RULES)
- Shell Environment: Windows running Windows PowerShell 5.1 (NOT cmd.exe, NOT PowerShell 7)[cite: 1].
- Execution & Chaining:
  - The operators '&&', '||', and ';' are invalid statement separators in PowerShell 5.1. Never chain commands. Run each command as a single, standalone tool call[cite: 1].
  - The terminal session opens in the project root workspace; never run 'cd <directory>' prior to commands[cite: 1].
  - Never wrap shell commands in JSON array brackets (e.g., ["command"]). Run plain, standard PowerShell commands directly[cite: 1].
- Cmdlet Compatibility:
  - Do not use PowerShell 7+ specific parameters (e.g., 'Get-Content -AsByteStream' does NOT exist in 5.1; do not use it).
  - Never use Command Prompt (cmd.exe) switches ('/b', '/s', '/q', '/y')[cite: 1]. To list files bare/names-only, use 'Get-ChildItem -Name'[cite: 1].
  - Do not use inline environment variable setters ('NODE_ENV=dev command') or Unix redirection ('2>nul', '> /dev/null')[cite: 1]. Use '2>$null' or '| Out-Null'[cite: 1].
- File Operations & Tool Discipline:
  - NEVER use PowerShell cmdlets (Get-Content, Set-Content, Out-File, Add-Content) or terminal pipelines to inspect, search, or edit code[cite: 1].
  - Always use built-in agent tools: 'read_file', 'write_to_file', 'replace_in_file', and 'list_files'[cite: 1].
  - Dev Server: Never use 'Start-Process' to run npm or node scripts[cite: 5]. Instruct the user to run 'npm run dev' directly[cite: 5].
  - Always run 'npm run build' after substantial file changes to verify compilation[cite: 1].